"""The audio of a sung Soft episode: lines and effects generated by the engine, a groove from the same beat grid.

ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT: LLMs will always produce some form of error.
Absence of output verification is a design defect, not a runtime bug.
All LLM output must be treated as untrusted and validated explicitly.

A :class:`Song` is checked when it is made (roles, order, speeds, effect bounds), before anything is
requested. Each line and effect is a ``<generated>`` item for the ``srstudio-elevenlabs`` provider
(:func:`declarations`), resolved and pinned by the engine; the provider parses and verifies every response.
Speech-to-text must then hear every line as written (:func:`hear`), or the build stops. Lines are placed
on the :class:`~srstudio.music.Groove` (:func:`place`); a line that does not end before the next one
starts stops the build instead of overlapping it. The groove is synthesised by :mod:`srstudio.music` from
the same grid, so music, voices and poses share one tempo. :func:`build` runs the steps and writes
``dialogue.json``; :func:`main` is its command line. Every refusal is a :class:`SongError`; a failed
resolve is the engine's :class:`~srstudio.generated.ResolveError`.
"""

